================================================================================
FINAL DETAILED REPORT (Gap 3 Closure Attempt)
================================================================================

OBJECTIVE:
Verify whether the Screw form Q and Groskin CCM form τ represent the same Weil 
explicit-formula quadratic form in different bases.

HYPOTHESIS: If true, then basis-independent invariants (spectrum, inertia, trace,
determinant, λ_min) must match, even though the basis representations differ.

METHODOLOGY:
1. Assembled both Q and τ at matched conductor c≈3 (a=0.549).
2. Tested with dimension-matched pairs: Q(m modes) ≈ τ(N) where 2N+1=m.
3. Computed basis-independent invariants for both forms.
4. Attempted numerical recovery of change-of-basis P via eigenvector Procrustes.
5. Assessed Charisma tier: Report (numeric evidence) vs Handle (proven equivalence).

KEY FINDINGS:

1. INERTIA SIGNATURE MISMATCH (critical, disqualifying)
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Q(5 modes, 5×5):   inertia (4, 1)  — 4 positive, 1 negative
   τ(N=2, c=3, 5×5):  inertia (5, 0)  — all positive-definite
   
   Q(7 modes, 7×7):   inertia (6, 1)
   τ(N=3, c=3, 7×7):  inertia (7, 0)
   
   Q(9 modes, 9×9):   inertia (8, 1)
   τ(N=4, c=3, 9×9):  inertia (9, 0)
   
   PATTERN: Q always has exactly (dim-1, 1) inertia.
            τ is always fully positive-definite (dim, 0).
   
   THEOREM: Congruence transformations (τ = P^T Q P) preserve inertia. 
   An inertia mismatch of this magnitude is IMPOSSIBLE under any basis change.

2. MATHEMATICAL CONSEQUENCE:
   If inertia signatures differ by (0, 1) as they do here, then
   τ ≠ P^T Q P for any invertible P.
   ⟹ The forms CANNOT be equivalent on the same space.

3. ADDITIONAL EVIDENCE OF MISMATCH:
   • Trace: Q ≈ 1.8-6.0, τ ≈ 1.7-6.4 (rough agreement but not quantitative)
   • Determinant: both ≈ 10^-11 to 10^-14 (both nearly singular)
   • λ_min: Q has 1 small negative eigenvalue, τ is strictly positive
   • Basis recovery: Procrustes alignment gives residuals ~1.0 (complete failure)
   • Spectrum: eigenvalue distributions are qualitatively different

4. CROSS-CHECKS:
   • Tried different c values (c=2, 5, 13): inertia mismatch persists
   • Tried -Q: doesn't help (inverts inertia but τ is still all-positive)
   • Scaled variants: don't resolve the fundamental inertia incompatibility

